## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of cross-account export patterns, least-privilege IAM, and auditability in AWS.

## Key Concepts

- STS AssumeRole for cross-account access
- S3 PutObject with tenant isolation and SSE-KMS
- Audit trails via CloudTrail and SNS
- Idempotent export and data integrity checks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example of initiating STS assumeRole and using temporary credentials
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const sts = new AWSSTS();
async function exportData() {
  const r = await sts.assumeRole({ RoleArn: 'arn:aws:iam::<customer>:role/ExportRole', RoleSessionName: 'ExportSession' }).promise();
  const s3 = new AWS.S3({ accessKeyId: r.Credentials.AccessKeyId, secretAccessKey: r.Credentials.SecretAccessKey, sessionToken: r.Credentials.SessionToken });
  await s3.putObject({ Bucket: '<customer-bucket>', Key: 'exports/tenant-id/export.csv', Body: 'data' }).promise();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle key rotation and trust policy changes?
- How would you test failure modes (expired credentials, insufficient permissions) and retries?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-region, multi-account DR with strict IAM boundaries and automated failover.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-region replication (S3 CRR, DynamoDB Global Tables)
- Route 53 failover with health checks
- Per-tenant IAM roles with least privilege and explicit denies
- IaC automation and DR testing

## Code Example

```terraform
# Minimal Terraform snippet for Route53 failover
resource "aws_route53_health_check" "region_a" {
  fqdn = "api.example.com"
  type = "HTTPS"
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "primary" {
  name = "api.example.com"
  type = "A"
  zone_id = var.zone_id
  set_identifier = "RegionA"
  failover_routing_policy {
    type = "primary"
    health_check_id = aws_route53_health_check.region_a.id
  }
  alias {
    name = aws_lb.region_a.dns_name
    zone_id = aws_lb.region_a.zone_id
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "secondary" {
  name = "api.example.com"
  type = "A"
  zone_id = var.zone_id
  set_identifier = "RegionB"
  failover_routing_policy {
    type = "secondary"
    health_check_id = aws_route53_health_check.region_b.id
  }
  alias {
    name = aws_lb.region_b.dns_name
    zone_id = aws_lb.region_b.zone_id
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify data consistency after failover?
- What monitoring alerts would you add?
